rious. Which is worse? Hard to decide. Perhaps we can say we remain with B but want to explore C further.\n\nWe could also ask a tool for more info on Candidate D's reliability or attention. But we can also just make a contribution.\n\nGiven the process, we should state our current recommendation. Let's maybe keep B as recommendation but note that C's reliability and crew atmosphere are strong and need discussion. So we can say we still support B but we need to compare with C.\n\nThus: \"I agree with Agent 2's recommendation for B, but I think we should also consider Candidate C because of his perfect reliability and positive crew atmosphere, which may offset his communication issues.\" That is a contribution.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: B is very conscientious, handles stress well; C is known to be 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, can make correct decisions quickly. Then implication: we should compare B and C.\n\nVote: Candidate B.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
